    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d131">

                <pb facs="0225" n="145" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg145"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-01-07"><hi rendition="#italic">January 7,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Conger reports that a memorandum has been left with him by the Russian
                    minister reporting three attacks by American sailors on Russian soldiers at
                    Niuchwang, one of the latter being wounded, and <pb facs="0226" n="146"
                        xml:id="pg146"/> reporting Admiral Alleexieff as saying that he fears a
                    continuance of such conduct will compel him to take severe measures to protect
                    his soldiers, and that henceforth he will disclaim all responsibility for
                    resultant consequences; that relations between Russian and other officials there
                    are much strained; and suggesting that the commander of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Vicksburg</hi> be instructed to use extra efforts to
                    restrain his men.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
